simulate_schedule takes AT MOST ONE entry per contiguous run of
flags (slice 17 — the rule that makes the rotation null valid). The
frozen ts_momentum_v1 flagged 2934 / 1260 / 1258 bars that formed
1 / 1 / 3 runs, so it scheduled 1 / 1 / 3 trades. The numbers above
are the same diagnostic for a signal that fires on the sign CHANGE
instead: flags merge only where the windowed return oscillates
across zero on consecutive bars.

